ENTRY 11498 {"id":11498,"kind":"pi.tool-result","messages":[{"role":"toolResult","text":"packages/orchestrator/src/sweep.ts:13: * Anything else is left alone: unlabelled claims (the e2e Phase 1 claim `e2e-phase1`), `control-<n>` labels of\npackages/orchestrator/src/kube.ts:27:/** Label that ties a SandboxClaim to the API session (or `control-<id>` for the test-only control sessions). */\npackages/orchestrator/src/main.ts:78:    return rows[0]?.id ?? `control-${String(conversationId)}`;\npackages/orchestrator/test/sweep.test.ts:65:  it(\"never touches an unlabelled claim, a control-session label or a name outside pi-conv-<n>\", () => {\npackages/orchestrator/test/sweep.test.ts:70:        { name: \"pi-conv-61\", sessionLabel: \"control-61\", createdAt: ago(600) },\ndocs/decisions/0002-orphan-sweep.md:29:Everything else is left alone: unlabelled claims (the e2e Phase 1 claim `e2e-phase1`), `control-<n>` labels of the\n        warmPool,\n        connectivity: \"in-cluster-service\",\n        authToken: token,\n      });\n    } catch (error) {\n      log(\"claim-failed\", { claim: claimName, message: errorMessage(error) });\n      throw error;\n    }\n    log(\"claim-ready\", { claim: claimName });\n    // Credentials for a repo session's commands only; plain sessions get nothing here. The token travels through the\n    // pi-env protocol to the daemon, never through the bridge process environment (bridge-launcher derives its own claim's token and drops the master).\n    const shellEnv = await this.#hooks.shellEnv?.(conversationId);\n    return connectSandboxEnv({\n      claimName,\n      namespace,\n      cwd: WORKSPACE,\n      id: `pi-env:${claimName}`,\n      bridgeCommand: [process.execPath, BRIDGE_LAUNCHER],\n      ...(shellEnv === undefined ? {} : { shellEnv }),\n    });\n  }\n   118\t  /** Creates the conversation and its sandbox claim, then submits the script as the first input. */\n   119\t  async startSession(script: Script): Promise<{ id: number; claim: string }> {\n   120\t    const conversation = await this.#harness.createConversation(\n   121\t      {\n   122\t        ownership: { kind: \"ownerless\" },\n   123\t        agent: { model: { provider: \"faux\", modelId: \"faux-1\" }, cwd: WORKSPACE },\n   124\t      },\n   125\t      context,\n   126\t    );\n   127\t    const id = Number(conversation.id);\n   128\t    await this.#sandboxes.ensure(id);\n   129\t    await conversation.submit(\n   130\t      { type: \"input\", content: JSON.stringify(script), requestId: `start-${String(id)}` },\n   131\t      context,\n   132\t    );\n   133\t    log(\"session-started\", { id, claim: claimNameFor(id) });\n   134\t    return { id, claim: claimNameFor(id) };\n   135\t  }\n","isError":false}]}
ENTRY 11521 {"id":11521,"kind":"pi.assistant","messages":[{"role":"assistant","text":"## Findings\n\n### 1. Failed control-session creation can leak a sandbox\n- Severity: low\n- Confidence: high\n- Location: packages/orchestrator/src/host.ts:128\n- What happens: If sandbox creation partially succeeds and then fails, or submitting the first input fails, the request returns without the conversation ID and without deleting the claim. A retry creates a new conversation and claim. The orphan sweep explicitly excludes control-session claims, so the abandoned resources are not reclaimed by it.\n- Evidence: `await this.#sandboxes.ensure(id);` is followed by `await conversation.submit(...)` with no cleanup on failure.\n- Fix idea: Clean up the sandbox on failed creation, and provide recovery for a process crash between claim creation and returning the ID.\n\nEND-OF-REPORT"}]}
DONE
